@host = https://localhost:7097

### Happy path — processed successfully; no replica traffic
POST {{host}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 49.99,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "shouldFail": false
}

### Forced failure — dead-lettered after retries; copied to payments-queue-deadletter, payments-audit, payments-alerts
POST {{host}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 49.99,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "shouldFail": true
}

### Invalid amount — dead-lettered via ArgumentOutOfRangeException; same replica fanout as above
POST {{host}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 0,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "shouldFail": false
}

### Slow payment — holds the delivery 20s. While it runs, drop the connection from the broker
### (docker exec <rabbit> rabbitmqctl close_all_connections demo) and watch the redelivery with
### DeliveryCount=1; do it again and the third delivery (count 2 = MaxBrokerDeliveries) is dead-lettered
### by the poison guard without running the handler (quorum queues only).
POST {{host}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 10,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "shouldFail": false,
  "processingDelayMs": 20000
}
